# scripts/opcount: sort N generated entries, the most severe first; the
# cost of one entry is the slope between the two sizes, so reading and
# start-up cancel only in part: both sizes read, sort and print. The
# control is the hand Go program with the same parse, the same sort (the
# same median-of-three quicksort with an insertion tail, the same range
# stack and scan guards) and a concrete compare written lazily, and the
# same print (CONSTRAINTS C4).
unit entry
sizes 20000 200000
input self -gen {n}
args -by severity
control examples/triage/testdata/control
